%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:nocc-rto -- a timeout retransmits the segment, and the window stays at its largest value.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; the comment of
each algorithm module names its behavior. The claim of TcpNoCongestionControl (its NED comment): no congestion control;
the window is always the largest.

The class nocc-rto: TcpNoCongestionControl::processRexmitTimer() retransmits one segment and
keeps the window. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates "nocc" from the other algorithms, which set the window
to one segment at a timeout.

Host under test: host1, with TcpNoCongestionControl, without SACK and without TLP
(preconditions); host1 sends 100000 bytes at 0.2 s, and the tap drops the 15th data segment the
first time. Observation: level 1 and 2, the timer of RFC 6298 retransmits the segment, within
1.6 s and so before the fixed timeout of 2 s of DumbTcp, and host1 signals no window below 1e9
bytes, which the other algorithms do.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: nocc-rto
%# value: "TcpNoCongestionControl"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassNoCongestionControlRto")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(never(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                             .filterValueAtMost(1e9)
                             .describe("a window below 1e9 bytes")
                             .within(4.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .nth(2)
                  .describe("the retransmission of the 15th segment, by the timer")
                  .within(1.6));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassNoCongestionControlRto compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpNoCongestionControl"    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
*.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassNoCongestionControlRto: PASS
